Interactions with independent neutral third world countries have been increased:

- Interactions with Nepal in the economic bloc will only be profitable if there is a trade agreement with China or India;
- Becoming members of the new economic union could include leftist countries such as: Myanmar, Laos, Cambodia, South Yemen, Libya, Sri Lanka;
- South Yemen will require oil development and investment to join the ranks of the new bloc;
- Sri Lanka, Myanmar and Laos will require additional subsidies upon membership in economic blocs allocated for their development;
- Cambodia also requires additional subsidies upon membership in the bloc, which could be cancelled with support for its offshore oil production;
- When reforms are rolled back, Libya can become part of an economic bloc with a diplomatic reputation above 70 and 3.0 coins;
- With more liberal and reformist policies, United Yemen and Thailand will be able to join the new bloc and will leave when their diplomatic reputation exceeds 40.0 coins;
- Many Asian countries have the additional option to start or resume trade with a player country if they fulfil certain actions (e.g. the required diplomatic reputation or not being in the same bloc as the USSR).
- Countries with civil war can join an economic bloc created by the player. Depending on the winning government, the conditions of interaction will differ (for example, with right-wing governments, diplomatic reputation must be below 35.0);

Enjoy the game!

"Jovic & Associates" update

- The chain of events for the military coup in Yugoslavia has been substantially reworked;
- Gorbachev now has more options to retain power when playing as Yugoslavia;
- Added new answer choices to some old events;
- Events when playing as HDZ are more personalised;
- Some endings have become more adaptive to current world events;
- Added new endings for Yugoslavia and some republics;
- Added the ability to view the leading politician and party in the republics of Yugoslavia;
- The combat system has been made more complex;
- In some cases, the map will be more adapted to the events taking place;
- More countries can now influence internal Italian affairs (and not only);
- Turkey and Cyprus can be contacted;
- Small edits on balance in eventing, modifiers and ministers;
- For every bug removed, 2 new bugs added.

Welcome back to the game, dear friends!

This free major update contains:

1. JUGOSLAVIA:
The new update "Milosevic and Markovic's Kosovo Vacation" for the dlc "Discord in Yugoslavia" will bring big changes to the game balance:
- more than 20 new endings that will more strongly personalise your eventual outcome of the changes in the Yugoslav republics;
- new investors in the socialist countries from other countries have been found;
- a new path for the Union of Reformist Forces of Yugoslavia, which could become a new unifying 
force in the Yugoslav space;
- more projects for the future territorial organisation of Yugoslavia were added; 
- with the help of leading Yugoslav engineers, each Yugoslav region now has its own unique buildings with its own effects;
- Yugoslav and national ministers were given a preventive talk at the UDBA, after which they could change the vector of their work;
- some ministers also found time to visit the photographer and received updated portraits close to game time;
- Ibrahim Rugova was released from the MIA department, resulting in significantly increased interaction with the insurgency;
- Albanian irredentists have also been released from prison;
- Milosevic would no longer simply put up with his second role in the party and his special conditions;
- Vojvodina is no longer a "silent province";
- The XIV Congress is now held continuously, and republican delegations are voting for individual motions with greater reluctance. The results of your votes will also lie in the draft of the new Yugoslav constitution. Or not;  
- the position of the PDD among the Bosnian opposition may now become more precarious;
- the Balkan commonwealth may now evolve into something more, depending on the actions of the SFRY;
- USSR 2.0 has been resolved;
- reliable communications have been established at army headquarters so that generals are not harassed by endless calls about attacks;
- more licences for independent media have been issued, which may have caused public reaction in the modifiers to change;
- the opposition radio is also no longer jammed and republican cassettes now have more than communist music;
- many new bugs have been added to replace the old ones;
- as well as a large number of achievements of varying degrees of difficulty;

2. HUNGARY:
- The event results on Hungary's threats have been redone.

3. ALBANIA:
- a new answer option in the Albanian event on economic reforms.

4. GENERAL:
- A new result of the removal of Xiaoping in China.

We wish you a pleasant transformation of Yugoslavia!
